findings.citation_text:
4-602.13 General surfaces throughout the facility were soiled and in need of cleaning, including but not necessarily limited to, the following:
1. counter under and around the tea dispenses and soda machine in the lobby (sticky splash and debris);
2. cabinet beneath drink counter in lobby (general buildup/debris)
3.surfaces around the soda machine at the drive thru (sticky splash); 
4. cart across from the soda machine in the drive thru (grease and dust accumulation);
5. prep table next to fryers (general buildup and food debris - under equipment and on lower shelf);
6. outer surfaces of bulk onion, salt, and meat spice storage bins (food debris/general buildup);
7. shelf holding bulk onion, salt, and meat spice storage bins (food debris/general buildup); and
8. walkin cooler shelving (mold/debris - especially around tomato storage).
Clean the aforementioned items. Nonfood contact surfaces shall be cleaned at a frequency necessary to eliminate buildup of grease, food splash and general debris.

findings.comment:
750.800b - The following food contact surfaces were soiled:
A) pepsi and mountain dew diffusers on left soda machine (mold) - taken to dish are to be cleaned and sanitized;
B) can opener blade (food debris);
C) ice machine (mold between top of baffle and surface above).

Clean and sanitize food contact surfaces between uses/as needed, up to every 4hrs after continuous use for in-use equipment and utensils such as knives, can opener, stem thermometer, etc.

750.800b - The following food contact surfaces were observed to be soiled:
A) soda nozzle diffusers (mold);
B) tongs in fry basket from previous operating day (food debris);
C) lids/inner surfaces of seasoning salt and salt shakers (buildup);
D) can opener blade (general buildup);  and
E) inside ice machine - on and around the baffle & inner surface of door (mold & general buildup/splash).
Items A thru D were taken to the dish area during inspection to go through ware washing process.

Clean food contact surfaces between uses/as needed, up to every 4hrs after continuous use, to prevent cross contamination and eliminate buildup of debris.

750.800e - The following non-food contact surfaces were observed to be soiled:
A) metal cart by drive thru (grimy buildup);
B) wire shelf of prep table next to fryers (grease);
C) front ledge of fryers in front of cooking oil (food debris);   and
D) walkin cooler shelves (buildup).

Clean non-food contact surfaces daily/as needed to eliminate buildup of debris.
